      "author": "Dan Goodin",
      "published": "2026-08-05T22:35:20Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Vulnerabilities in Baseboard Management Controllers (BMCs) enable persistent, OS-agnostic root access below the hypervisor layer.",
        "Flaws in out-of-band management firmware allow remote code execution and hardware backdoors across major OEM server platforms.",
        "Security teams must strictly isolate BMCs on dedicated management VLANs, restrict IPMI access, and audit out-of-band firmware integrity."
      ]
